; THE EMBERDEEP MINE (Phase 38N1) — the realm's first PRODUCTION settlement, and the second market the
; economy has been waiting for since 38F.
;
; It exists to be the other side of the Embermarket's prices. Ash Dunmore has been saying since 38L
; that "there's a mine east of here they say is opening again. Emberdeep. If it does, I'll be buying
; ore by the cartload"; this is that mine, and the two shops in it are deliberately a SOURCE and a
; SINK rather than two more stalls:
;   Bregan Holt weighs ore at the lowest markup in the realm (1.15) and barely buys.
;   Marta Quill pays the most for food anywhere (0.62 fraction, `food` specialty) and sells nothing.
; A settlement whose merchants accepted everything would be the town square with different scenery,
; which is the whole failure 38G was parked to avoid.
;
; ⚠️ The cell is placed at Center (56, 0, -10), abutting the town hub's 60 m floor which ends at
; x = 30: a 52 m floor centred at x = 56 starts exactly there. (An older note here said 99; that was
; wrong and the arithmetic it quoted was for a placement the region file never had.) Every transform
; in this file is LOCAL. The road in is from the WEST, so local -x is toward the town.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav — geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; navmesh, so an NPC would walk straight through the mine head. The two merchants deliberately do not.
;
; ⚠️ NO RAISED GROUND (38K). CharacterBody3D has no step-up, so the whole cell is flat and its height
; comes from a 6 m mine head, 2.2 m boulders and the ore heaps — from props, never from terrain.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THE 2026-08-28 LAYOUT REBUILD REPLACED. One 34 x 16 yard band across the middle of the cell with the mine head at
; the east end of it: every building, merchant, cart and ore heap the mine had was inside that band and
; the whole place was legible from the gate. A mine that reads at a glance is a diagram of a mine.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW IS A LOOP, and the walk out is not the walk in:
;   x -26..-14, z -5..1   THE DEFILE. The road in, squeezed to 6 m between two spoil-boulder walls.
;                         You can see nothing of the workings from it. The waystone is at its far end.
;   x -17..1, z 0..19     THE WEIGHING YARD, opening SOUTH off the defile — the reveal is a turn, not
;                         a straight. Bregan's scales on its west side, Marta's company store on its
;                         south, carts and stacked crates between them.
;   x -23..-15, z 10..20  THE MINERS' REST, fenced, off the yard's west flank: the shift fire and
;                         nothing to trade. A pocket rather than a route.
;   (-4,8) -> (8,-4)      THE HAUL ROAD, north-east out of the yard between the ore heaps.
;   x 3..15, z -9..-3     THE CUT. Six metres wide, ore seams and boulders both sides. The pinch.
;   x 10..26, z -18..0    THE PIT HEAD — a bowl ringed by spoil, the mine head against its north-east
;                         wall at (20, -14) facing back down at whoever just cleared the Cut. This is
;                         the landmark and the only place in the cell you can see the whole of.
;   x 11..17, z -1..19    THE SPOIL TRACK and its link west at z = 17, closing the loop back into the
;                         yard: timber stacks, waste boulders, nothing to buy.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_mine"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.3
cell_height = 0.3
agent_height = 1.8
agent_radius = 0.6
agent_max_climb = 0.3
agent_max_slope = 42.0

[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_ember"]
albedo_color = Color(0.62, 0.22, 0.08, 1)
emission_enabled = true
emission = Color(1, 0.45, 0.12, 1)
emission_energy_multiplier = 3.0

[sub_resource type="SphereMesh" id="Mesh_coals"]
radius = 0.13
height = 0.26
radial_segments = 8
rings = 4

; Ground skin. NO COLLIDER (see the step-up note above): a 6 cm lip is something the player catches on.
; The 2026-08-28 layout rebuild: seven worked surfaces instead of one 34 x 16 band. Together they form a LOOP — yard,
; haul road, cut, pit head, spoil track, spoil link, back to the yard — so the mine is somewhere you
; go round rather than a corridor you go up and come back down.
